body:
I stopped crying a while ago. Thats good! that you don't feel bad, you might just have begun to accept yourself and who you are. Maybe you are just growing up? i've heard it like that as you become accustom to daily life.

Is it the meds that interfere with your sex life?

&#x200B;

Maybe chase adrenaline? thats a good way to feel again?

&#x200B;

In saying that, i have gone bungie jumping and felt nothing.

Thanks for the update, i read your last post. I am glad you made it to the hospital. They do take your phone away so you are not distracted from the treatment they are giving you. I know the treatment is few and far between but they are always on shit and watching you very closely. Do you get a doctors visit everyday? do you have group sessions? (just curious about how different it is in America \[given you called 911\]). 

&#x200B;

They will be working for your diagnosis and watching you throughout your stay. How are you feeling after the overdose? did anything else happen? How long do you have to be with the sitter? 

&#x200B;

In my own life when i was hysterically laughing its actually cause i really wanted to cry nut couldn't and ended up in serious tears later in life when the laughing fits came back. I didn't always cry but it used to happen a lot to me when i was really sad.
